he budgets of the  United Kingdom Germany Japan and only 12  billion dollars less than the entire  military budget of Russia so anybody who  says Oh Trump's making a small  adjustment you know doesn't know what  they're talking about or they're trying  to pull the wool over your eyes and what  he's planning to do which is a little  different from recent presidencies he  wants to take $1 a billion dollars fifty  four billion dollars out of domestic  programs to match the 54 billion he  wants to put in the military now this is  an outrage but it's also an opportunity  to build coalitions because so many  people are going to be affected he's  going to eliminate 19 agencies and he's  got a the initial hit list of programs  that they were going to get rid of  included the National Endowment of the  Arts  Nessun down with humanities corporation  for public broadcasting legal services  for the poor the u.s. Institute of Peace  Planned Parenthood AmeriCorps the  Appalachian Regional Commission works  works almost entirely in Trump country  so anyway that initial hit list is about  three billion dollars which is one-half  of 1% of the Pentagon budget so it's  peanuts compared to the Pentagon and it  just gives you a sense of how deep  they're going to have to cut on the  domestic side to counterbalance this  proposed build-up and some of the  proposed cuts are just hard to fathom  31% cut of the Environmental Protection  Agency 29% of the State Department this  is the guy who likes to make deals who's  going to make the deals when there's no  State Department they're going to get  rid of eight billion dollars in  low-income block grants of various sorts  pay for low-income heating pay for  housing for the homeless pay for job  training programs that's less than the  cost of one of the twelve ballistic  missile submarines that are part of this  trillion dollar build up and then states  going to be cut twenty nine percent but  UN humanitarian programs will be cut  even deeper 